# basics

This directory contains the scripts of the shell basics project. Each script is exactly two lines long: a shebang followed by one command, and every file ends with a new line.

## Scripts
- 0-current_working_directory: prints the absolute path name of the current working directory.
- 1-confused_smiley: displays a confused smiley using quotes and escaping.
- 2-bring_me_home: changes the working directory to the home directory without using shell variables.
- 7-movethatfile: moves the file betty from /tmp to /tmp/my_first_directory.
- 11-lists: lists all files, including hidden ones, of the current directory, the parent directory, and /boot, in long format.
- 16-clean_emacs: deletes all files ending with a tilde in the current directory.

## Restrictions
Backticks, double ampersand, double pipe, and semicolons are not allowed in the scripts.
EOF
